<description>
Recolor teal pixels yellow when their 2-pixel-block distance from the pink marker lies inside the marker-centered hourglass.

Input structure
A black-bordered grid contains one noisy teal field, one 2x2 pink marker,
and full black separator lines along exactly one axis.

Rule
Remove the full black rows and columns to get compressed coordinates.  From
the 2x2 pink marker, measure distances in two-pixel blocks along each axis.
The separator-line axis is the narrow axis of the hourglass; the other axis
is the opening axis.  A teal pixel becomes yellow exactly when both distances
are nonzero and the narrow-axis distance is no greater than the opening-axis
distance.

Key insight
The black separator lines identify which direction the hourglass opens, so
the vertical-stripe and horizontal-stripe examples use the same distance
predicate after compression.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "teal foreground pixels, one 2x2 pink marker, and full black separator lines along one axis",
  "transform": "remove the separator lines for coordinate measurement; recolor a teal pixel yellow when its nonzero marker-centered 2-pixel-block distance along the separator axis is no greater than its nonzero distance along the opening axis; preserve all other pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    border: 1-pixel black frame on all sides
    separator_axis: rows or cols (exactly one), evenly spaced with period 3 (2 content + 1 separator)
    num_separators: 4-7 along chosen axis [observed]
    non_sep_axis: even number of content pixels (no separators), range 10-18 [observed]
    compressed_dims: both even, 10-18 per axis [observed]
  colors:
    background: BLACK (0), source: TEAL (8), marker: PINK (6), output_recolor: YELLOW (4)
  marker:
    shape: solid 2x2 block of PINK
    compressed_position: at even row and even col [observed], not on boundary of compressed grid
  source_fill:
    interior cells (non-border, non-separator) are ~90-95% TEAL, rest are BLACK holes
    hole_rate: 5-12% of interior cells [observed]
    holes are scattered randomly, may appear anywhere including marker rows/cols
  transform:
    compress grid by removing separator lines; compute 2-pixel-block distance from marker center along each axis
    TEAL pixel becomes YELLOW when both distances > 0 and separator_axis_distance <= opening_axis_distance
    this creates an hourglass/diamond pattern centered on the marker, opening along the non-separator axis
    holes and marker are preserved unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction
  steps:
    1. Pick separator_axis (row or col), n_seps in 4-7, non_sep_axis content size (even, 10-18)
    2. Build raw grid dimensions from structure: sep_axis = 2 + (n_seps+1)*2 + n_seps, non_sep = content+2
    3. Fill border rows/cols and separator lines with BLACK
    4. Place 2x2 PINK marker at even compressed coords, not touching compressed boundary (>=2 from each edge)
    5. Fill all remaining interior cells with TEAL
    6. Randomly set 5-12% of non-marker interior cells to BLACK (holes)
